From 78e4ceeb0358a8c42c3a79033834d3b5aad3ec21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:54:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): hub CPU/cap final gate with an independent full
 sample under admission.lock; origin claims skip worker load formula [daveey]

- Advisory lock-free pre-check before the Board lease (ruling 5); final gate under admission.lock
  takes a real 1 s /proc/stat sample, rechecks whole-host cap and lease deadline (ruling 1 override).
- Origin claiming its own policy card no longer uses the worker load1/CPUs formula (ruling 2).
- Eight overflow queue reason codes; claimed event records the consumed sample.
- No automatic structural origin repin: legacy origin reply still applied, new no_eligible_worker keeps fence (ruling 9).
- Real-sample test asserts the whole sample ran with the lock held, hold <= 2.5 s, and the measured
  0.5 s BUSY_WAIT_S chat-turn outcome matches the hold interval.
